      "description": "Watch Standard Liege vs Cercle Brugge highlights and goals from Jupiler Pro League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 10, 2026. The Jupiler Pro League delivered another captivating chapter on August 10, 2026, as Standard Liège and Cercle Brugge faced off in a high-stakes encounter. Both sets of supporters expected a tactical battle, and the players on the pitch certainly lived up to the billing. Early Intensity and the Breakthrough The match began with a physical edge, as the referee was called into action early to maintain control. Adnane Abid and Valy Konate both received yellow cards in the first 40 minutes as challenges flew in. The deadlock was finally broken in the 41st minute when Dante Vanzeir turned provider, setting up Lukas Mondele for a clinical finish that gave the home side the momentum. Eckert Takes Control Just as the first half drew to a close, the game shifted dramatically. In the fifth minute of added time, Adnane Abid found Dennis Eckert , who made no mistake in doubling the lead. The interval did little to slow the home side's rhythm, as Eckert struck again in the 48th minute. Assisted by Casper Nielsen , the forward secured his second goal of the match, effectively putting the contest out of reach for the visitors. Late Response and Final Whistle The closing stages saw a flurry of substitutions as both managers looked to adjust their tactics. Cercle Brugge continued to fight and managed to pull a goal back in the 88th minute through Christiaan Ravych , but it proved to be a mere consolation. The referee brought the proceedings to a halt in the 91st minute, confirming a dominant performance for the hosts in a match defined by clinical finishing and tactical discipline."
